+/*
+ * Developer-only scripted test driver. It is enabled only when the
+ * PARALLACTION_AUTOTEST environment variable points at a command file.
+ * One command per line:
+ *   wait <frames>            let the game run
+ *   move <x> <y>             move the mouse (screen coordinates)
+ *   click <x> <y>            left click
+ *   rclick <x> <y>           right button down/up
+ *   key <char>               press a key (use F5 for the in-game menu)
+ *   shot <file.png>          dump the current screen
+ *   cursorshot <file.png> [<screen.png>]
+ *                            log the pointer set with the HD renderer (size, how it was made) and dump
+ *                            it (ARGB); with a second file also the screen with the pointer drawn at
+ *                            the mouse position (the backend draws the pointer, shot does not see it)
+ *   loc <location> <part>    jump to a location (BRA) / location (NS)
+ *   zones                    log the zones of the current location
+ *   framelog on|off          log every displayed frame (time, scroll, render cost)
+ *   fullredraw               compose the next frame from scratch
+ *   verifyscroll on|all|off  compare every scrolled (all: every) frame with a full redraw (SHIFTCHECK)
+ *   flag <NAME>              set a global flag (BRA)
+ *   item <name>              add an object to the inventory (BRA)
+ *   hintlog                  log the objective the hint key would show (BRA)
+ *   conf <key> <value>       set a configuration value (application domain)
+ *   gui <step>...            open the ScummVM menu and run steps inside it:
+ *                            w:<ms> wait, k:<char|down|up|enter|esc> key,
+ *                            shot:<file.png> dump the GUI overlay
+ *   manual <step>...         press M (BRA) and run the same steps inside the manual, plus
+ *                            c:<x%>,<y%> click, rc:<x%>,<y%> right click,
+ *                            d:<x1%>,<y1%>,<x2%>,<y2%> drag, wh:<n> wheel (n > 0 down),
+ *                            k:left|right|pageup|pagedown|home|end|space|m
+ *   modal <step>...          run the same steps in the next window that opens by itself
+ *                            (the end titles, BRA): the times count from now
+ *   quit                     quit the engine
+ */
+
